-- הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 "תשלום קצובת נסיעה", מהדורה 7 (26.1.2023)
-- Edition 7 of the Accountant-General's travel-allowance instruction. Its
-- change table names what it adds to edition 6: the weekly trip home of an
-- Arab, Druze or Circassian employee who moved 70 km or more (2.1.3), "from
-- 1 August 2022" (2.3.2), the volunteer (2.3.5), the income-tax deduction
-- and gross-up (2.7), annex A's volunteer and annex B's payroll rules. What
-- it repeats from edition 6 it takes from that file, by import.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `kitzuvat-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-in-force`
IMPORT `2022-11-17_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v6`

-- Tariffs: the notice's (`travel fares`, read off the notice in force by
-- `the travel allowance on the route` below). No rule here rounds
-- (convention rounding.default).

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: ‘בעל’ here is the holder of a
-- post or of a service or assigned car (‘בעל רכב צמוד’, ‘בעל נהג צמוד’),
-- not a husband; the instruction sets one travel allowance for every
-- employee, man or woman, and does not distinguish between them.

-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: ‘חודש סיום העסקה’ here is a
-- month in which the travel allowance is paid pro rata (2.1.5), not notice
-- of dismissal or resignation.

§ `הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 תשלום קצובת נסיעה — מהדורה 7`

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- 1.1, as in edition 6: the employees of the ministries and their
-- auxiliary units.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1
GIVEN `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `edition 7 applies to` `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IF
    `edition 6 applies to` `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit`

-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 Further payments in Eilat and the Negev are the notice "תשלומים לנוסעים / עובדים באילת ותוספת ערבה", which the corpus does not hold; no rule here.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/p2 The instruction's purpose; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-4 A pointer to annex A, whose definitions the rules below cite; no rule.

§§ `2.1 זכאות לקצובת נסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 The heading "זכאות לקצובת נסיעה"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.1.1, 2.2.1 and its four cases, and annex A's definitions 1 and 7, as
-- in edition 6 (2.1.1, 2.2.1): an employee who needs transport is
-- entitled, unless a State arrangement carries him all month, or he has an
-- assigned car or driver, or is absent a calendar month or more.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_7 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-4 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 7` m IF
    `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 6` m

-- 2.1.2 and annex A's definition 4, as in edition 6: one residence.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4
`the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 7` MEANS `the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 6`

-- 2.1.3, new: notwithstanding 2.1.2, an Arab, Druze or Circassian employee
-- who moved residence 70 km or more from the permanent home is refunded, in
-- addition to the allowance, once a week, a trip from the workplace to the
-- permanent home, at a single "bus" or "train" fare, by the employee's
-- report. One trip a week, one way, as the clause and annex B's code 1360
-- ("עבור נסיעה בודדת ... פעם בשבוע") both print it.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
`the trips home a week, edition 7` MEANS 1

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `trips a week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the weekly trips to the permanent home` f m `trips a week` IS
    IF m's `relocated 70 km or more as an Arab, Druze or Circassian employee`
    THEN f's `single fare` TIMES `trips a week` TIMES m's `weeks with a trip to the permanent home`
    ELSE 0

-- 2.1.4, as edition 6's 2.1.3.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-4
`the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 7` MEANS
    `the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 6`

-- 2.1.5, its two tariffs and annex A's definitions 2-3, as edition 6's
-- 2.1.4: in a month not fully worked, the lower of the monthly ticket and
-- the daily ticket times the days actually worked.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5__pnt_2-1-5-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5__pnt_2-1-5-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 7` f m IS
    `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 6` f m

-- 2.1.6, as edition 6's 2.1.5: a partial allowance in proportion to the
-- trips made otherwise than by a State-funded arrangement.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-6
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 7` amount m IS
    `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 6` amount m

§§ `2.3 קביעת זכאות לקצובת נסיעה בעקבות רפורמת דרך שווה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.3.1-2.3.2, as in edition 6, 2.3.2 adding "from 1 August 2022": every
-- means of public transport is refunded, the train included, by the
-- notice's rules.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-2
`the train is refunded with every other means of public transport, edition 7` MEANS
    `the train is refunded with every other means of public transport, edition 6`

-- 2.3.3, as in edition 6: the equalisation supplement of those taken into
-- the State service by 31.7.2022 is the notice's.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-3
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`, `the equalisation the notice sets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 7` m `the equalisation the notice sets` IS
    `the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 6` m `the equalisation the notice sets`

-- 2.3.4, as edition 6's: the hourly employee, the daily tickets for the
-- days travelled, no more than the monthly ticket. 2.3.5, new, with annex
-- A's definition 5 (a volunteer as the takshir's chapter 16.6, section
-- 16.611, defines one): the volunteer, in the same words.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-4 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-4/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hourly employee's or volunteer's allowance, edition 7` f m IS
    `the hourly employee's allowance, edition 6` f m

GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid by the days travelled, edition 7` m IF
        m's `kind of employee` EQUALS `an employee paid by the hour`
    OR  m's `kind of employee` EQUALS `a volunteer`

GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance for travel to work, edition 7` f m IS
    `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 7`
        (IF `paid by the days travelled, edition 7` m
         THEN `the hourly employee's or volunteer's allowance, edition 7` f m
         ELSE `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 7` f m)
        m

-- 2.3.6 and annex A's definition 6, as edition 6's 2.3.5: five monthly
-- tickets, cancelling every other entitlement.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_6
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the blind employee's allowance, edition 7` f IS
    `the blind employee's allowance, edition 6` f

-- 2.3.7, as edition 6's 2.3.6 ("on the way to work and back"): 128
-- shekels a month in addition.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7/p2
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 7` m IS
    `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 6` m

§§ `2.4 קצובה בגין נסיעה בשבתות וחגים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.4.1-2.4.2, as in edition 6: the daily ticket for each Sabbath or
-- holiday day the employee came, not with a service or personal car nor in
-- an office with a shuttle.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-2
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 7` f m IS
    `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 6` f m

-- 2.4.3: with the monthly allowance, within "the payment cap, as in
-- section 2.3 above"; as in edition 6, section 2.3 states no cap
-- (F-2023-01-26_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v7-a). The reading adopted:
-- the cap is an input.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER @desc the cap 2.4.3 sends to section 2.3, which states none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 7` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    min (`the allowance for travel to work, edition 7` f m PLUS `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 7` f m)
        `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`

`the caps section 2.3 states, edition 7` MEANS EMPTY

`section 2.4.3 refers to a cap section 2.3 does not state, edition 7` MEANS
    `the caps section 2.3 states, edition 7` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 2.4.3 refers to a cap section 2.3 does not state, edition 7`

`why 2.4.3 gives no figure for the cap, edition 7` MEANS
    `the text is silent` "F-2023-01-26_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v7-a"

-- The month's allowance, as edition 6 builds it, with 2.1.3's weekly trips
-- home "in addition". The blind employee's replaces every other, those
-- trips included ("מבטלת כל זכאות אחרת המפורטת בהוראה זו").
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance, edition 7` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 7` m THEN 0
           IF m's `blind` THEN `the blind employee's allowance, edition 7` f
           OTHERWISE `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 7` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`
                     PLUS `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 7` m
                     PLUS `the weekly trips to the permanent home` f m `the trips home a week, edition 7`

