-- an unreported move is collected back from the day of the move.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `reporting a move, edition 7` IS `reporting a move, edition 6`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-5__cls_2-5-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `refreshing the details, edition 7` IS `refreshing the details, edition 6`

§§ `2.6 יישום במערכות השכר`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.6.1-2.6.2 and annex B §1, as in edition 6.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-1 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `paying through the payroll, edition 7` IS `paying through the payroll, edition 6`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-6__cls_2-6-2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `paying outside Malam, edition 7` IS `paying outside Malam, edition 6`

§§ `2.7 ניכוי מס הכנסה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.7.1: the travel allowance is taxable income; taxes are deducted by law.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `withholding income tax, edition 7` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `withhold income tax from the travel allowance`

-- 2.7.2-2.7.3: the tax is grossed up on the part above 527 shekels a month
-- for an employee employed 5 days a week, above 620 for one employed 6.
-- The edition gives no threshold for any other week
-- (F-2023-01-26_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v7-b); the reading adopted:
-- as printed, no gross-up for such a week (convention reading.as-printed).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-3
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the gross-up threshold, edition 7` m IS
    BRANCH IF m's `days worked a week` EQUALS 5 THEN JUST 527
           IF m's `days worked a week` EQUALS 6 THEN JUST 620
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN allowance IS A NUMBER, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the part grossed up, edition 7` allowance m IS
    CONSIDER `the gross-up threshold, edition 7` m
    WHEN JUST t THEN `the part above` allowance t
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-7__cls_2-7-3
GIVEN allowance IS A NUMBER, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `travel-allowance duty`
DECIDE `grossing up the tax, edition 7` allowance m IS
    IF `the part grossed up, edition 7` allowance m GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `gross up the tax on the travel allowance` `part`
               PROVIDED `part` EQUALS `the part grossed up, edition 7` allowance m
    ELSE FULFILLED

`a week of four days has no gross-up threshold, edition 7` MEANS
    `the gross-up threshold, edition 7` (`a four-day week, edition 7`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a week of four days has no gross-up threshold, edition 7`

`why 2.7 gives no gross-up threshold for another week, edition 7` MEANS
    `the text is silent` "F-2023-01-26_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v7-b"

§§ `3-4 מסמכים ישימים ונספחים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-2 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-3 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-4 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-5 The applicable documents (the takshir's chapters 28.3 and 16.6, the form, the two notices); a source list, no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-3 The list of annexes; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 Annex A's title "הגדרות"; its definitions are cited by the rules that use them.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 Annex B's title; its clauses follow.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2/t1 How each kind of payment is reported in "Malam Sachar" (event 226, code 4820, event 041, code 971 multiplying by 5, code 901, code 1360 for the single weekly trip home, sum 1077) and the salary code it is paid under; payroll coding, no entitlement of its own.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_3 The codes of the public-transport lines are the notice's; a pointer, no rule.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/t1 Annex C, the table of the editions' changes; a record, no rule.

§§ `התעריפים — the notice in force`

-- The edition reads the monthly free pass and the daily free pass, the single fare; here they are read off the notice
-- "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית" in force on the month's day (HOD
-- 13.4.2.1, `taarifei-nesia-in-force`), for the employee's route. Where
-- the notice prints no tariff the edition reads, there is no answer.
GIVEN r IS A `travel route`, d IS A DATE @desc the month's day
      m IS A `travel month`
      `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance on the route, edition 7` r d m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    CONSIDER `the travel fares of the route on` r d TRUE TRUE FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 7` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`)

-- The equalisation supplement the notice in force sets, on the route's
-- monthly free pass.
GIVEN r IS A `travel route`, d IS A DATE
      m IS A `travel month`
      x IS A NUMBER @desc the allowance paid before the reform, every component included
      `the highest allowance of 2022` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel-allowance equalisation on the route, edition 7` r d m x `the highest allowance of 2022` IS
    CONSIDER `the tariffs of the route on` r d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rt THEN
        CONSIDER rt's `route monthly pass`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST monthly THEN
            CONSIDER `the equalisation supplement in force on` d x monthly `the highest allowance of 2022`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s THEN JUST (`the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 7` m s)

§§ `Worked examples`

`placeholder fares, edition 7` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 300
        `daily free pass`       IS 20
        `single fare`           IS 15
        `intercity single fare` IS 0

`edition 7 pays` m MEANS `the travel allowance, edition 7` `placeholder fares, edition 7` m 1330

`a four-day week, edition 7` MEANS
    `travel month` WITH
        `kind of employee`                                  IS `a monthly employee`
        `needs transport from home to work`                 IS TRUE
        `a full month of work`                              IS TRUE
        `days actually worked`                              IS 17
        `share of trips by a State-funded arrangement`      IS 0
        `has an assigned car`                               IS FALSE
        `has an assigned driver`                            IS FALSE
        `has a service or personal car`                     IS FALSE
        `absent a calendar month or more`                   IS FALSE
        `blind`                                             IS FALSE
        `in a full position`                                IS FALSE
        `lives where there is no public transport`          IS FALSE
        `Sabbath and holiday days reached`                  IS 0
        `the office runs a shuttle`                         IS FALSE
        `lives in a national-priority locality`             IS FALSE
        `travels on lines with a monthly pass`              IS TRUE
        `travels intercity individually`                    IS FALSE
        `relocated 70 km or more as an Arab, Druze or Circassian employee` IS FALSE
        `weeks with a trip to the permanent home`           IS 0
        `days worked a week`                                IS 4
        `taken into the State service by 31.7.2022`         IS FALSE

#ASSERT `edition 7 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) EQUALS 300

-- 2.3.5: a volunteer who came 8 days, the daily tickets.
#ASSERT `edition 7 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `a volunteer` 8) EQUALS 160

-- 2.1.3: four weekly trips home at a single fare of 15, in addition.
`a relocated employee's month, edition 7` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 4 0
#ASSERT `edition 7 pays` `a relocated employee's month, edition 7` EQUALS 360

-- 2.7.2: an allowance of 600 for a 5-day week is grossed up on 73; for a
-- 6-day week on nothing.
#ASSERT `the part grossed up, edition 7` 600 (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) EQUALS 73
#ASSERT `the part grossed up, edition 7` 600 `a four-day week, edition 7` EQUALS 0

-- On 1.2.2023, a monthly employee of 22 days on `a 30 km route` (the
-- Tel Aviv codes before the reform, 30 km by bus after it): the edition's
-- allowance on the tariffs the notice in force prints.
#ASSERT `the travel allowance on the route, edition 7` `a 30 km route` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2023) (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) 1330 EQUALS
    JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 7` `the route's fares on 1.2.2023, edition 7` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) 1330)

`the route's fares on 1.2.2023, edition 7` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 255
        `daily free pass`       IS 28
        `single fare`           IS 12
        `intercity single fare` IS 0
